## 12. Inherited findings — disposition

Every open finding carried in by [`proposal.md`](./proposal.md) §4, with where it is closed.

| # | Disposition |
| --- | --- |
| **F-1** | **Dissolved.** C-2 no longer does skip arithmetic — it measures the fetch directly (R-AGD-004) |
| **F-2** | **Closed.** Keys are seeded by migration; six in-repo precedents (§5) |
| **F-5** | **Closed.** `activePopulation`, `ceiling`, `ceilingBreached` are summary fields; dry-run C-3 reports instead of aborting; the rollout plan carries the restore step (design §11) |
| **F-8** | **Closed, and narrowed to its one live form** — `CARNET_TOO_LONG` skips (R-AGD-002 AC.1) |
| **F-10** | **Closed.** EX-3 counts active rows only (R-AGD-003 AC.4) |
| **F-11** | **Closed.** §10 maps every rule to a gate; each is required to be observed red |
| **W-1** | **Converted into C-4** — an abort, not an assumption (R-AGD-004 AC.4/AC.5) |
| **W-6** | **Dissolved with F-1** — drift no longer feeds an equality test |
| **W-9** | **Accepted and narrowed.** Chunked, id-ordered writes; **no isolation level is set, because the codebase has none anywhere** — deviating here would be inventing a convention inside a destructive spec (RSK-4) |
| **W-10** | **Avoided.** The `app_secrets` write goes through `manager.getRepository(AppSecret)`, so `AppSecretRepository` — and its `Scope.REQUEST` `CurrentUserUtil` dependency — is never injected (R-AGD-005) |
| **RSK-6** | **Carried, not fixed.** Recorded as OQ-2; the cascade closes it for retired users only |
| **NEW-1** | **Answered:** seed migration (§5) |
| **NEW-2** | **Answered:** yes, a skipped member still shields (R-AGD-002) |
| **NEW-3** | **Dissolved:** C-2 no longer counts carnets as a completeness measure |
| **NEW-4** | **Dissolved on evidence:** collapse key ≡ match key (R-AGD-002, dissolution table) |
| **OQ-6** | **Answered:** dry-run first, default enabled *(user ruling 2026-09-15)* |
| **OQ-7** | **Re-asked and re-confirmed:** absence still deactivates *(user ruling 2026-09-15)* |
| **OQ-D2** | **Answered and corrected:** `app_config`; the K-016 TTL warning was misattributed (§5) |

